Fix first-enter push when git-lfs is installed

git cat-file --batch-check interpolates %(atom) only. Unlike
for-each-ref, it copies pretty-format hex escapes such as %09
through as literal text. The LFS object scan treated that format
as tab-separated, so first-enter recover_push panicked with
"malformed line: <oid>%09commit%09<size>" whenever a leftover
image branch was a strict descendant of the fetched remotes.

Use the default space-separated batch-check format instead.
